WEBVTT

NOTE seasonal-profiles: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.369
A small set of profiles,
one per condition,

V0-2
00:00:05.469 --> 00:00:09.550
is easier to run a season with than
a long list of dated snapshots.

V1a-1
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.268
Plan what goes in the five slots.

V1a-2
00:00:16.368 --> 00:00:19.930
The tab lists five named profile
slots for each Lynx course.

V1b-1
00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:25.329
A short list stays readable a year later.
Applying a profile is a course-wide

V1b-2
00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:29.933
recalculation, so treat it as a planned
change rather than a quick switch.

V2a-1
00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:41.201
Applying rewrites the target of every
station in the profile and recalculates

V2a-2
00:00:41.301 --> 00:00:45.543
their suggestions; stations not
in the profile keep their targets.

V2b-1
00:00:46.553 --> 00:00:51.613
Doing it the evening before leaves you the
next morning to read the new suggestions

V2b-2
00:00:51.713 --> 00:00:56.103
against a fresh scan. Apply, then
review the next morning’s suggestions.

V3a-1
00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:06.480
A profile changes targets,
and targets change deficits.

V3a-2
00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.921
Scan the Suggested column for stations
that jumped to the cap — those are the

V3a-3
00:01:11.021 --> 00:01:15.250
ones where the new target is a long
way from where the station actually is.

V3b-1
00:01:16.213 --> 00:01:19.453
New targets, new suggestions —
review before pushing.

V4a-1
00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:30.963
The push dialog is the same as any
other day. The difference is the size of

V4a-2
00:01:31.063 --> 00:01:35.593
the change set: a profile switch usually
queues most of the course at once.

V4b-1
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.500
A profile switch queues a
large push. Review it as one.
